The `\rowcolor` command in LaTeX is used to color a specific row in a table. This command needs the "colortbl" package to be used in the preamble of the document. 

Here's how you can use this command:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{colortbl}

\begin{document}

\begin{table}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|l|}
\hline
\rowcolor{red} Column 1 & Column 2 & Column 3 \\ 
\hline
Data 1 & Data 2 & Data 3 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\end{document}
```

In this example, the first row of the table will be filled with the color red. The colors available will depend on the color model you are using. If you don't get the color you specified, it may be because you did not include the right package for that color model.

